.SS "Image (\fBPort\fP port, boolean copyPixels = \fR\fBCopyPixels\fP\fP)"

.PP
Create an independent snapshot or a live image of an offscreen surface\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIport\fP An open \fBPort\fP returned by \fBGraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIcopyPixels\fP Defaults to \fBpdg\&.CopyPixels\fP (true): copy the current RGBA pixels into an independent image\&. With \fBpdg\&.SharedSurface\fP (false), retain the shared drawing surface: subsequent \fBPort\fP drawing is visible the next time the image is drawn, without constructing another image or uploading pixels when both use the same graphics context\&. Literal booleans remain supported; an omitted or undefined flag uses CopyPixels\&.
.RE
.PP
Creates an \fBImage\fP with the port's dimensions and transparency\&. Throws an Error for an onscreen port and TypeError for a non-boolean copyPixels\&. Use new with this constructor\&.

.PP
Both kinds of image remain usable after the source port closes\&. Closing a port with live images prevents further drawing through that port but retains its final surface until the last live image is released\&. Closing the underlying graphics context preserves its final pixels for surviving images\&. \fBDrawing\fP does not depend on which clip rectangle was active when the image was created: the image always represents the whole surface\&.

.PP
Pixel reads and serialization of live images read the current contents\&. Serialized images are snapshots and do not restore a connection to a \fBPort\fP\&. \fBDrawing\fP across independent graphics contexts, or drawing a live image back into its own source, uses a pixel snapshot\&. Calling \fBsetTransparentColor()\fP on a live image converts that image to an independent snapshot before applying the color key\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires a graphics-enabled build\&. Shared images retain graphics memory until released, even after closeGraphicsPort()\&. An image's opacity is independent of the port\&. 

.PP
API stability: 2 — Evolving\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const surface = pdg\&.gfx\&.createOffscreenPort(new pdg\&.Rect(128, 128));
if (!surface) throw new Error('Could not allocate drawing surface');
const live = new pdg\&.Image(surface, pdg\&.SharedSurface);
surface\&.drawEllipse(new pdg\&.Point(64, 64), 40, 40,
    new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.fillColor('red')\&.lineStyle(pdg\&.lineStyle_None));
// Drawing live now shows the red circle; further surface drawing updates it too\&.
const frozen = new pdg\&.Image(surface, pdg\&.CopyPixels);
// frozen keeps this circle even when the surface changes\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBGraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort()\fP, \fBPort::drawImage()\fP, \fBgetPixel()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::CopyPixels\fP\&.
